{"data":{"id":29587,"name":"Wormhole","symbol":"W","slug":"wormhole","category":"token","description":"## What is Wormhole?\nWormhole is the asset transfer infrastructure through which all digital assets move. As capital markets, stablecoins, and real-world assets transition onchain, Wormhole provides the secure, universal interoperability platform that enables them to flow seamlessly between blockchains. Since launching in 2020, Wormhole has become the leading interoperability platform, connecting more than 40 blockchains and facilitating over $60 billion in value in more than 1 billion cross-chain messages.\nInstitutions including BlackRock, Apollo, Hamilton Lane, VanEck, and Securitize rely on Wormhole to power tokenized assets and multichain capital markets, while protocols like Circle (USDC), Uniswap, Lido, Pyth, and Jupiter depend on it to enable movement of assets and data across ecosystems. By bridging the gap between traditional finance and crypto, Wormhole is not just an interoperability protocol, it is the critical infrastructure layer for the future of global capital markets.\n\n## What is unique about Wormhole?\nWormhole was the industry’s first cross-chain bridge, a true pioneer in the industry back when “multichain” was not a widely accepted trend. Today, Wormhole’s uniqueness lies in its security, decentralization, and open source code. Wormhole’s decentralized set of 19 validators include globally-recognized entities such as Google Cloud and other top validator firms. Wormhole’s model was independently selected by the Uniswap Bridge Assessment Committee as the most secure option for cross-chain bridges, citing its validator quality, decentralization, and architecture.\nIn addition, Wormhole has one of the industry’s most robust bug bounty programs and employs end-to-end encryption to safeguard transactions. These measures ensure Wormhole’s infrastructure can be trusted for the largest-scale use cases in both DeFi and traditional finance.\nWormhole also holds open source ethos as a standard for development, unlike some competitors who operate with closed source code similar to Web2 companies like Facebook.\n\n## How is Wormhole used?\nWormhole provides tools for users to bridge assets and developer tools for blockchains, apps, and tokens:\n[Portal](https://portalbridge.com/) – A user-facing bridge powered by Wormhole, offering low fees, low latency, and strong security guarantees. The most used bridge in the history of the industry.\nNTT (Native Token Transfers) – The leading multichain token standard that enables tokens to exist multichain with a single supply, critical for stablecoins and institutional assets.\nMessaging – Developers can integrate cross-chain messaging directly via the Wormhole SDK.\nQueries – Secure pull-based, cost-efficient data access across chains.\nIntents – An SDK extension that allows users to express desired outcomes while solvers handle execution, creating faster, more intuitive cross-chain UX.\nMultiGov - The industry’s first multichain governance system, allowing users to vote across any chain.\nThese capabilities are already used by institutions like Securitize to issue multichain tokenized funds (including BlackRock’s BUIDL, Apollo, VanEck, and Hamilton Lane vehicles), by DeFi protocols to unify liquidity across chains, by blockchains like Solana and Base, and by wallets and dApps to deliver seamless multichain experiences.\n\n##What’s the utility of the W token?\nThe W token is the native asset powering the Wormhole platform. Holders can stake their tokens in governance on the W Dashboard, participate in governance processes that shape the network’s future, protocol upgrades, fee models, and connection management. W will also be the means of generating and redistributing network fees and revenue back to token holders. Additional token use cases such as staking for Queries and new chain connections are also on the product roadmap.\nW is natively multichain, enabled by Wormhole’s NTT framework, allowing it to move seamlessly across supported ecosystems.\n\n## What are the real-world applications of Wormhole and its products?\nWormhole serves as the connective layer of the internet economy, enabling use cases far beyond traditional bridging:\nInstitutional Tokenization – Powers tokenized treasuries, funds, and securities from BlackRock, Apollo, Hamilton Lane, VanEck, Securitize, Mercado Bitcoin, Janus Henderon, and more.\n\n\nStablecoins & Payments – Enables transfer of Circle USDC, USDT, Metamask’s mUSD, M0, Agora AUSD, Transfero (BRZ, ARZ), and others across multiple chains.\n\n\nDeFi & Governance – Enables Uniswap DAO’s cross-chain governance, supports liquidity across PancakeSwap, Lido, Pyth, Synthetix, and more.\n\n\nWallets & User Apps – Empowers multichain wallets like Phantom, Backpack and numerous consumer-facing apps.\n\n\nThese use cases illustrate Wormhole’s dual role: serving as infrastructure for both Wall Street-scale financial innovation and crypto-native ecosystems.\n\n## What key events have there been for Wormhole?\n2020 – Launched Wormhole as the first Ethereum–Solana bridge, backed by the Solana Foundation.\n\n\n2021–2023 – Expanded into a multichain platform with products like the Wormhole SDK, Connect, Queries, and NTT.\n\n\n2024 – Selected by Uniswap as the most secure cross-chain bridging option (LayerZero was denied use by Uniswap due to security risk); Validator set expanded to include Google Cloud; hardware acceleration partnership with AMD; launch of the W token.\n\n\n2025 – Became the interoperability layer for institutional tokenization, powering billions in multichain tokenized funds from BlackRock, Apollo, Hamilton Lane, and VanEck via Securitize.\n\n\nThese milestones mark Wormhole’s evolution from a crypto-native bridge to the institutional-grade infrastructure layer for global capital markets.\n\n## What is the technology behind Wormhole?\nWormhole deploys a bridge contract on each connected chain. Validators (called Guardians) run full nodes, observe events, and collectively sign Verified Action Approvals (VAAs). Relayers then deliver these signed messages to target chains for execution to deliver the data or value to the destination chain. This architecture provides a secure, scalable foundation for the transfer of all digital assets, setting the standard for interoperability infrastructure.\n\n## Who are the founders of Wormhole?\nWormhole is developed by a decentralized network of contributors including the Wormhole Foundation, Wormhole Labs, Asymmetric Research, and xLabs. Wormhole was incubated at traditional finance giant Jump for two years prior to decentralization of the core contributor teams.\n\n## Related Links\n\nTo learn more about Wormhole, its products and ecosystem, visit:\n\n*   [Wormhole website](https://wormhole.com)\n\n*   [Wormhole blog](https://wormhole.com/blog)\n    \n*   [Wormhole community](https://wormhole.com/community/hub)\n    \n*   [Wormhole docs](https://wormhole.com/docs/)\n    \n*   [SDK](https://wormhole.com/products/sdk)\n    \n*   [Portal](https://portalbridge.com/)\n","dateAdded":"2024-03-29T04:25:44.000Z","actualTimeStart":"2024-04-03T11:30:00.000Z","status":"active","isBn":1,"subStatus":"normal","notice":"","alertType":2,"alertLink":"","latestUpdateTime":"2026-10-19T06:45:00.000Z","watchCount":"96260","watchListRanking":406,"dateLaunched":"2020-10-07T00:00:00.000Z","latestAdded":false,"tags":[{"slug":"collectibles-nfts","name":"Collectibles & NFTs","category":"CATEGORY","status":1,"priority":3},{"slug":"defi","name":"DeFi","category":"CATEGORY","status":1,"priority":3},{"slug":"interoperability","name":"Interoperability","category":"CATEGORY","status":1,"priority":3},{"slug":"dao","name":"DAO","category":"CATEGORY","status":1,"priority":5},{"slug":"ethereum-ecosystem","name":"Ethereum Ecosystem","category":"PLATFORM","status":1,"priority":3},{"slug":"coinbase-ventures-portfolio","name":"Coinbase Ventures Portfolio","category":